from pathlib import Path
import json,statistics
r=Path('docs/homepage-refinement/phase-11a5');e=r/'evidence/stage-b';images=json.loads((e/'integrated-images.json').read_text());qa=json.loads((e/'responsive-qa.json').read_text())
intro='Updated 2026-11-17. Conditional Stage B integration only. Hero remains schematic until final visual approval.\n\n'
perf='# Photography performance report\n\n'+intro+'## Method and limits\n\nHeadless Chromium on the local Next production server, fresh browser contexts and disabled browser cache, DPR 1. Two desktop samples at 1440×900 without throttling and two mobile samples at 390×844 with 4× CPU throttling, 150ms latency, 1.6Mbps down/750Kbps up. Same measurement harness before and after. The after run was repeated without concurrent browser diagnostics. Local server image-optimizer caches were warm from verification; this does not measure first-ever server-side encoding, remote hosting or field CWV. Two samples are descriptive, not statistical evidence of an improvement.\n\nInitial values are taken after network idle and 2.5s; full traversal switches to chemicals, scrolls through all sections and waits. It does not visit every solution. The separate delivered-images inventory also visits spares. Native source bytes and review-document bytes are not website transfer bytes.\n\n| Profile | Build | Median observed initial LCP, ms | Median initial subresource transfer, bytes | Median traversed image encoded bodies, bytes | Observed full-traversal CLS |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\n'
for profile,mobile in [('Desktop',False),('Mobile',True)]:
 for stage in ['before','after']:
  d=json.loads((e/f'performance-{stage}.json').read_text());runs=[x for x in d['runs'] if x['mobile']==mobile]
  lcp=[x['initial']['metrics']['lcp'][-1]['start'] for x in runs if x['initial']['metrics']['lcp']]
  imagebytes=[sum(t['encoded'] for t in x['final']['resources'] if t['type']=='img') for x in runs]
  cls=[sum(t['value'] for t in x['final']['metrics']['shifts'] if not t['input']) for x in runs]
  perf+=f"| {profile} | {stage} | {statistics.median(lcp):.0f} | {statistics.median(x['initialResourceTransferBytes'] for x in runs):,.0f} | {statistics.median(imagebytes):,.0f} | {', '.join(f'{n:.5f}' for n in cls)} |\n"
perf+='\nPhotographs increase payload over line schematics. The unchanged hero is still a text/schematic composition; these measurements do not demonstrate hero-photo performance. Differences in small local LCP values are noise, not a claimed loading improvement. No production Core Web Vitals or zero-CLS guarantee is asserted. No page errors were recorded in the sample runs. The harness automation round-trip measurement is not INP.\n\n## Local production assets\n\n| Placement | Native JPEG | WebP master | Master dimensions |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n'
for i in images:perf+=f"| {i['id']} | {i['originalBytes']:,} B | {i['bytes']:,} B | {i['width']}×{i['height']} |\n"
perf+=f"\nSix WebP masters total {sum(i['bytes'] for i in images):,} bytes, versus {sum(i['originalBytes'] for i in images):,} original JPEG bytes. This is source-to-derivative storage reduction, not a claim that every master downloads at once. Existing responsive Next Image delivery and lazy loading remain active. Hero receives no new resource or priority change. Review boards/original working files are outside public/ and not loaded by the app.\n\n"
if (e/'delivered-images.json').exists():
 perf+='## Actual local responsive responses\n\nCache-disabled, DPR 1, reduced-motion delivery inventory (not the throttled timing benchmark). These are encoded response bodies, excluding headers; one entry per requested photo response.\n\n| Viewport | Source | Requested optimizer width | Encoded bytes |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n'
 from urllib.parse import urlparse,parse_qs
 for profile in json.loads((e/'delivered-images.json').read_text()):
  for im in profile['resources']:
   q=parse_qs(urlparse(im['url']).query);src=q.get('url',[''])[0]
   if '/images/industrial/' in src:perf+=f"| {profile['width']} | {src.split('/')[-1]} | {q.get('w',[''])[0]} | {im['bytes']:,} |\n"
perf+='\n## Tablet layout-stability observation\n\nThe required responsive capture recorded small startup shifts at 768px (~0.00798) and 1024px (~0.00746), with 0 in the 390/1440/1920 captures. Detailed sources in tablet-shifts.json identify the hero editorial moving 8px and footer moving 16px at startup, consistent with the existing hero 112px fallback versus measured 96px header variable. This is an inference from the entries and unchanged header/hero sizing code, not a measured pre-integration tablet comparison. No image-frame collapse was observed. The photography scope preserves that header/hero behavior; do not hide this residual observation behind a universal zero-CLS claim.\n'
(r/'PERFORMANCE_REPORT.md').write_text(perf)
visual='# Photography visual QA\n\n'+intro+'## Actual homepage captures\n\nAll required screenshots show the production-build homepage with the six configured photographs, not a mock-up. The default earthmoving solution remains schematic by the rights hold; additional active-panel captures show chemicals/spares. Full-page captures use reduced motion and DPR 1 so every section remains static/readable. Existing normal-motion/parallax cleanup is covered by the complete browser suite. Device widths are Chromium emulation, not physical-device or screen-reader certification.\n\n| Viewport | Actual homepage | Horizontal overflow | Page errors | Observed capture CLS |\n|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n'
for q in qa:visual+=f"| {q['width']} | [capture](screenshots/homepage-integrated-{q['width']}.png) | {'None' if q['scrollWidth']<=q['width'] else 'Present'} | {len(q['errors'])} | {q['cls']:.5f} |\n"
visual+='''\nDesktop/mobile actual screenshots and detailed section captures were opened for inspection. PH02 is component-focused; its public derivative is physically cropped at native x=700, y=54, 2800×3360 before encoding to 1600×1920, excluding the worker partial profile rather than implying a portrait release. PH10 retains a rear-view figure and long shaft, making it distinct from PH02. PH05 keeps the process towers; PH07-B keeps the central neutral fastener; PH08 retains handling paths/equipment; PH11 retains silos/walkway. No colour treatment, new font or typography repositioning was introduced. All displayed images decoded successfully in responsive capture.\n\nExisting navy/white and amber/navy text remains outside these below-fold image frames, so photographs do not become text backgrounds. Captions use the existing light/dark section colours and remain legible. No caption clipping, horizontal overflow, collapsed frames or hero/header overlay collision was seen. The small tablet startup hero/footer movement is fully recorded in PERFORMANCE_REPORT.md; zero CLS at every width is not claimed.\n\nSolutions selection was exercised for both photos and all held schematic divisions. Active photo panel captures: [chemicals desktop](screenshots/solution-industrial-chemicals-1440.png), [chemicals mobile](screenshots/solution-industrial-chemicals-390.png), [spares desktop](screenshots/solution-consumables-spares-1440.png), [spares mobile](screenshots/solution-consumables-spares-390.png). Existing keyboard selection, focus, reserved panel geometry, reduced motion, mobile menu, navigation and quotation regressions passed. Error tests cover optimized-image failure recovering to schematic, then double failure recovering to accessible text without collapsing the frame.\n\n## Hero studies are separate\n\n[Final review board](FINAL_SELECTION_BOARD.html), [desktop](screenshots/final-selection-1440.png), [mobile](screenshots/final-selection-390.png). These are comparative crop/overlay studies, not the implemented hero or evidence of final in-page contrast acceptance. R1 has a distant machine; R2 explicitly proposes horizontal reflection. Final hero visual approval remains required. The original Stage A REVIEW_BOARD.html is historical and contains the now-rejected Built/Komatsu candidate; use FINAL_SELECTION_BOARD.html for the current decision.\n\n## Remaining acceptance\n\nThe six integrated photographs still require the user's final visual acceptance. PH01 requires candidate selection/approval; PH03/PH09 require new source-specific rights evidence or a separately approved replacement. PH04/PH06 intentionally remain labelled schematics. No stock scene is described as an actual Zieve facility, employee, customer, project or current inventory.\n'''
(r/'VISUAL_QA_REPORT.md').write_text(visual)
ready='# Phase 11A.5 — final readiness\n\n'+intro+'''**Conditional integration complete; ready for image review, not deployment or Phase 11B.**\n\n- Integrated six: **PH02, PH05, PH07-B, PH08, PH10, PH11**. PH07-B is the cleaner neutral fasteners alternative, documented against the original. PH02's displayed crop excludes the worker profile; PH10 shows a distinct long shaft/rear-view composition.\n- Remain schematic: **PH01, PH03, PH04, PH06, PH09**. PH04/PH06 by instruction; PH03/PH09 because source-specific brand/people conditions are unresolved. Direction approval was not treated as blanket commercial clearance.\n- Hero: original Built/Komatsu candidate rejected. Two replacement crop studies with original URLs/licence evidence are in [FINAL_SELECTION_BOARD.html](FINAL_SELECTION_BOARD.html) and [IMAGE_SELECTION_REPORT.md](IMAGE_SELECTION_REPORT.md). R1 is scenic with a small excavator; R2 is equipment-led but requires approval of horizontal reflection. Neither is connected to the app. Google Images was attempted but inaccessible; this limitation is recorded.\n- Six native originals were acquired, fully decoded, inspected and hashed; source/download links, modification/commercial conditions, optional attribution, local filenames, resolutions and intended-use assessments are in the source/licence registers. No separate release certificate or blanket rights warranty is fabricated. Contributor/publisher credits and stock provenance are visible.\n- Preserved all nine sections, original logo, typography/tokens, header/hero behaviors, layout/motion utilities, navigation, quotation form, inner pages and deployment configuration. No packages installed, purchases, permission requests, AI photos or deployment. Existing schematic fallback files/objects remain intact.\n\n## Verification\n\n- ESLint: passed.\n- Strict TypeScript: passed.\n- Production build: passed.\n- Unit/component tests: **43 passed / 12 files**.\n- Playwright: **126 passed**, desktop and mobile. Includes Phase 11A discovery/reflow, 200% root text, photo loading/failure and existing section/navigation/form behavior.\n- Actual homepage captures: **390, 768, 1024, 1440, 1920px**; no horizontal overflow or page errors in the capture inventory. Photo frames remained reserved.\n- Local before/after measurements and actual responsive payloads recorded. Photo payload increases over schematics; no causal LCP improvement or production CWV claim. Small tablet startup hero/footer shifts (~0.008 CLS) remain documented and outside the photography change.\n- Source integrity: existing changes limited to three media maps and relevant tests; header/hero/components/content/tokens/routes/logo/deployment unchanged. See evidence/stage-b/scope-integrity.json.\n\n## Files changed\n\nCreated src/config/industrial-photography.ts; six public/images/industrial/**/*.webp assets; tests/photography.test.ts; tests/e2e/photography.spec.ts; tests/e2e/media-routes.ts. Modified src/config/{introduction,solutions,industry}-media.ts; tests/{introduction,industries}.test.ts; tests/e2e/{introduction,solutions,industries}.spec.ts. Updated the seven required current reports, research follow-up, review board/screenshots/evidence, docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md and docs/CONTENT.md. No production component or CSS file was rebuilt.\n\n## Review needed\n\nChoose R1 or R2 (including its stated crop/reflection tradeoff), or reject both; review the six actual integrated placements for final visual acceptance. No additional permission is needed to keep PH03/PH09 on their current schematic holds. Any future replacement or paid acquisition needs its own approved source and appropriate rights. Stop here: no Phase 11B or deployment authorization is inferred.\n'''
(r/'FINAL_READINESS_REPORT.md').write_text(ready)
(r/'screenshots/README.md').write_text('''# Screenshot index\n\nCurrent actual production-build homepage: homepage-integrated-{390,768,1024,1440,1920}.png. Chemicals/spares active-panel captures: solution-{industrial-chemicals,consumables-spares}-{390,1440}.png. These include the six conditional photographs and all held schematics.\n\nCurrent hero/spares review studies: final-selection-{390,1440}.png and ../FINAL_SELECTION_BOARD.html. These do not modify the app hero.\n\nHistorical Stage A studies: research-board-* and REVIEW_BOARD.html include the now-rejected PH01 candidate. baseline-schematics-* show the unchanged pre-integration homepage. Do not confuse these with current acceptance evidence.\n''')
